      "topic": "Warship cabin subdivisions and bulk-heads",
      "quote_wikipedia": "In large warships, the cabin was subdivided into day and night cabins (bedrooms) by movable panels, called bulk-heads, that could be removed in time of battle to leave the cabin clear for the gunners to use the stern chasers several of which were usually stationed in the cabin."
